I worked on calculating how much it would cost to use an LLM API based on its usage. I created a program where details like the number of requests per day, input tokens, output tokens and API pricing are considered. Using these values, the program calculates the estimated daily and monthly cost. I also included RPM and TPM limits to check whether the application can handle the expected number of requests and tokens. Along with this, I added daily and monthly budget limits and a safety margin. The program displays the results and shows whether the estimated usage is within the given limits. Through this experiment, I understood why it is important to calculate API costs and plan usage before developing an AI application.
